Both evaluator issues are fixed and committed:

1. CLAUDE.md doc fix — the ReadModeGuardTool bullet no longer claims "plain > redirection is not caught". It now documents the actual behavior: bash commands are blocked by the destructive-pattern classifier OR safety::detect_write_command (write verbs touch, mkdir, `mv, cp, tee, truncate, sed -i, dd of=, install, ln` at token boundaries, plus >/>> redirection outside quoted regions; refusal names what matched).

2. Missing test added — `test_read_guard_bash_blocks_write_commands_refused_in_read_mode` in tool_wrappers.rs:
• Refuses tee /tmp/x and touch /tmp/x under read mode, asserting the error names read mode and says the command writes
• Passes both commands through when no mode is active (both sides of the boundary, per the Day 122 lesson)
• Uses the existing #[serial] + ReadModeReset RAII pattern to avoid poisoning the process-global mode flag

